From 49e716508610879fdbdedabce82118ad38f05412 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add master tune (A4 reference pitch 415.3-466.2 Hz)

Settings > Tuning > Master tune (Hz) sets the reference pitch of A4 in
0.1 Hz steps (default 440.0).

- Everything that makes sound follows it: synth and kit rows (waveforms,
  wavetables, samples, DX7, FM carriers and modulators), audio clips
  (pitch-shifted, tempo kept), CV outputs and external MIDI. Applied once
  per oscillator with an exact 64-bit multiply.
- Audio recorded on the Deluge at another tuning gets a 12-byte "mtun"
  chunk with that tuning. It is only shifted by the difference to the
  current tuning, and the pitch detection works relative to it, so it is
  never tuned twice. Other software skips the chunk.
- Live input used as an oscillator already sounds at the current tuning
  and is left alone.
- Changing it retunes notes that are already sounding: voices recalculate
  their pitch at their next render, CV is re-output, external MIDI is
  retuned.
- External MIDI tracks and MIDI drums get RPN 1 (Channel Fine Tuning) on
  every channel they play: right away when the tuning changes, before the
  first note on a channel that doesn't have it yet, and again after
  playback begins. The broadcasts are sent from a task, only while the
  DIN MIDI buffer has room, so they never overflow it or delay the notes
  playback starts with. Channels shared by several tracks or drums are
  tuned once. Nothing is sent while the firmware was never retuned.
- Stored as "masterTune" in CommunityFeatures.XML on the SD card (firmware
  that doesn't know it keeps it as an unknown setting). A value left in
  flash bytes 198-199 by earlier master-tune builds is migrated and those
  bytes are zero again once the settings file holds the value.
- At 440.0 Hz everything not recorded at another tuning is identical to
  the unmodified firmware.
- Project version set to 1.2.1 to match the release this is based on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
